---
/** About on screen; the CV's profile paragraph in print. */
import { leadershipYears } from "../data/skills";
import { careerYears } from "../data/jobs";
import { decadesInWords } from "../lib/experience";
import SectionHeading from "./SectionHeading.astro";
import TextPair from "./TextPair.astro";
---

<section id="about" aria-labelledby="about-h" class="flex flex-col gap-6 pt-24 print:gap-2 print:pt-0">
  <SectionHeading id="about-h"><TextPair screen="about" print="profile" /></SectionHeading>
  <div
    class="flex max-w-[760px] flex-col gap-4 font-sans text-[19px] leading-[1.65] text-prose print:text-[13.5px] print:leading-[1.6] print:text-ink"
  >
    <p class="print:hidden">
      I started coding for fun as a teenager — it grew into my main occupation. At 30, after years of autodidact training, I studied Software Engineering at the University of Applied Sciences Upper Austria in Hagenberg. At heart, I'm still a tinkerer.
    </p>
    <p class="print:hidden">
      {leadershipYears}+ years of leading and supporting engineering teams — always hands-on, always writing code myself. Today I build AI agents and agentic workflows for production and connect them with modern web apps and (legacy) systems. I help teams put coding agents to productive use without compromising on code quality.
    </p>
    {/* The CV words the counts ("over two decades", "more than 10 years"); the screen keeps the terminal's `N+ years`. */}
    <p class="hidden print:block">
      AI engineer building production-grade agents and agentic workflows that solve real problems. This is backed by over {decadesInWords(careerYears)} of hands-on full-stack engineering. Through more than {leadershipYears} years of leading engineering teams, I have always kept writing code myself. I like to get the most out of what's already there: connecting agents, modern web apps and legacy systems. I help teams put coding agents to productive use without compromising on code quality, while staying in control: writing code where it matters, set the architecture, review, and decide what goes to production.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
